{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And they hammered out the plates of gold</b> — In none of the work of the Sanctuary did he add to explain the method of craftsmanship how it was made, except here. And it would have been fitting for him to say, \"And they made the ephod of gold, blue, etc., the work of a skilled weaver; they made shoulder-pieces for it, etc.,\" for so is the way in all of them. And it is possible that he recounts here the innovation they devised with the threads of gold, for it was wondrous in their eyes that gold could be spun and twisted just as is done with wool and linen, for it had never been heard of until that day to do such a thing:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:22:13.596196539Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}